# CODEOWNERS — human ownership of the trust-critical surface.
#
# Rationale (docs/SPECIFICATION.md §12.2a, docs/CI-AND-TRUST.md §2a): if an agent could
# modify BOTH the code under test AND the verification workflow, the workflow could certify
# its own change. Required status checks do not help when the check is authored inside the
# PR. These paths therefore require review from a human owner. CODEOWNERS reviews use the
# BASE branch version of this file — helpful — but CODEOWNERS itself and the branch-protection
# settings still require controlled ownership on the platform.
#
# This file is necessary but NOT sufficient. Pair it with, in preference order:
#   1. an organisation-level required workflow, or
#   2. a reusable verification workflow in a separate, more tightly protected repo
#      (pinned by immutable commit SHA), or
#   3. a protected CI app whose verification logic lives outside this PR's writable tree.
# And on GitHub: protected `main`; required review + required status checks (`verify`,
# `mutants-critical`); "do not allow bypassing the above settings (include administrators)"
# ENABLED; and the bypass list VERIFIED EMPTY (not assumed — rulesets can contain bypass actors).
#
# The owner below is a sensible default (the repository owner). Replace or augment it with a
# dedicated reviewer or a protected team before any live phase.

